Final head is `7010ba500068cff1d49f9e211873871107b16008`. Since the zero-open-items review of `9f0a7d05ab2`, only the lazy-preparation regression fixture changed: it now actually invokes the policy assertion during preparation. All 11 real-router/cancellation cases pass, and the focused owner coverage totals 113 passing tests. Both committed lineage regressions fail on the exact parent and pass with the fix. Codex reviewed the fixture correction with no actionable findings.

The two previously reported items remain addressed as detailed in https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/198245#issuecomment-6853014549: (1) uncertain post-handler outcomes are nonretryable; (2) HTTP policy outages return 503. Their production code is unchanged. The PR body records the remaining local validation, including the sidebar browser test's startup timeout; no incomplete or failed check is called green.

@clawsweeper re-review
